e range of the function." :question/worked-solution "Cosecant is undefined at pi and at every n*pi, so (pi,-1) is not on its graph and those x-values are vertical asymptotes. It takes the value 2 where sin(x)=1/2."} {:db/id 17592186176548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aadfbfd-7e0d-5462-9403-7ec6f34bcd45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439867} {:answer/id #uuid "36512727-2b25-560b-a5ef-a6a4dca23d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36512727-2b25-560b-a5ef-a6a4dca23d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439868} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14982a7-98ac-5534-aa55-8a5040b1aa77" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3081db96-8e26-52e9-95d2-ce823865c78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439869} {:answer/id #uuid "0f14ba72-6dd9-5b85-8fb4-3a959179e0b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3081db96-8e26-52e9-95d2-ce823865c78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439869} :answer-field/id #uuid "632309ee-0c98-5584-910d-0b95c24c4b57" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b38f072-608f-59e8-ac23-79a3eeb7fa91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439871} {:answer/id #uuid "db27e3a1-ed43-5079-8562-a73f366e243b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db27e3a1-ed43-5079-8562-a73f366e243b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439872} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2616ba-1558-574f-a2d0-2541e9af7773" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440293}] :question/id #uuid "82d5c89d-6391-5689-957e-6be71174a415" :question/math-academy-id "q-65310" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$.\n- **II.** The function has a zero at $x = \\frac{π}{2}$.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $-1$ at $x =-\\frac{π}{2} + 2nπ$." :question/worked-solution "Cosecant is defined exactly when x is not n*pi, never equals zero, and equals -1 at -pi/2+2n*pi."} {:db/id 17592186238055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43695e61-1e83-5a72-9ff3-f9bf8f0ff41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437324} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9f1b84-1f9d-52ee-b77c-bb7cf2eaf5ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43695e61-1e83-5a72-9ff3-f9bf8f0ff41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437324} :answer-field/id #uuid "5985bcd7-8973-51f9-9c22-d1da25705334" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94f1f229-d949-5c5e-aaf2-e1aff529a00a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437326} {:answer/id #uuid "e88c8370-f864-5a65-8d5f-24e20ca5796f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94f1f229-d949-5c5e-aaf2-e1aff529a00a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437326} :answer-field/id #uuid "2613d71e-2edc-5912-80f7-8226169c47b5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcf21feb-caad-5f01-82f0-e33663c8dbc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437328} {:answer/id #uuid "8328e87e-23da-585d-b66e-42111af5c87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8328e87e-23da-585d-b66e-42111af5c87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437329} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5477318-3d23-52d5-9a55-05595aeaea30" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55643e28-3c44-53e1-a6da-d559974acbda" :question/math-academy-id "q-103811" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all positive real numbers.\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, the statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$ So, $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$ Hence, statement III is true."} {:db/id 17592186238056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437336} {:answer/id #uuid "36efe75c-8338-5448-b8b1-f0f24de49042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437336} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f359a76-6b4d-5ef4-8d92-7e15d488f261" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "434a0e71-1d31-5c13-a968-09b7e4ab49c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437338} {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437339} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e70be4-e476-5046-a564-3ee1193d0d78" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85984aac-915a-5905-a791-04f32942b8bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437340} {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437341} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cd87df-e0b6-57e0-879b-9a26805f19c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "048ceaff-1e4b-5807-8d50-fab96c1502f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103814" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- **II.** $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/06/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true."} {:db/id 17592186335824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e211abea-7b27-5a54-be2b-2776b824b945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/valu