blem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true."} {:db/id 17592186335825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438356} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f89c4d-da0d-58fc-ab37-efc5ed7f1053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438356} :answer-field/id #uuid "30435fb6-1037-57a8-b967-d652cdf699a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ebde88-a46b-560f-9b2d-c9311641fa24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438358} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438359} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa49081-1dec-5a36-ad7e-37cc67073211" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438360} {:answer/id #uuid "d95548b2-40ec-5ebf-b1ab-d29936ab04f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438360} :answer-field/id #uuid "168eb318-5e34-58b3-8153-3564c073e9ff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69d68c82-75d2-569e-bc5a-a35be8a71a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false."} {:db/id 17592186399398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437330} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dce793-5565-5d7f-905d-7cd04e4d56ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437330} :answer-field/id #uuid "a341d84b-92d9-5335-b0b9-fd13587dacad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74c41ab1-5221-54d6-bfb2-b2d2b1a66a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437332} {:answer/id #uuid "79a66b2d-395b-5d7a-972b-1551475dda80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74c41ab1-5221-54d6-bfb2-b2d2b1a66a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437332} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d83191a-11eb-57de-8d9a-63c9eb52fa02" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7478e7-5c82-57c4-9e23-eb0f7d938047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437334} {:answer/id #uuid "c4654fa4-c8d7-53b9-af56-adb9aeac3408" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e7478e7-5c82-57c4-9e23-eb0f7d938047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437334} :answer-field/id #uuid "548cb375-8481-538b-9ce6-63f0f2d26906" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4383ecaa-1c57-5705-8853-cba2341fc9fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-103812" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$\n- **II.** $y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function.\n- **III.** $x=15\\pi $ is in the domain." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements I and II are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement III is false."}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}